'''Vidal''' is a [[Balisca|Baliscan]] [[W:Automotive industry|automotive]] cooperative headquartered in [[Pujol]], [[Tartessia]] ([[Hesperia]]). Vidal maintains its main vehicle manufacturing facility at [[Fabrica Vidal I]] in [[Merced]], [[Cadaqués]]. The company operates multiple production and assembly plants overseas, notably [[Fabrica Vidal III]] near [[Nanporo]], [[Takamaiku]]. It manufactures passenger [[W:Battery electric vehicle|battery electric vehicles]] (BEVs) and [[W:Plug-in hybrid electric vehicles|plug-in hybrid electric vehicles]] (PHEVs) along with [[W:Electric bus|electric buses]] and [[W:Electric truck|electric trucks]]. It is the largest producer of automobiles in the [[Baliscan Confederation]], and one of the largest [[W:Electric vehicle|EV]] producers in the world.

Following the [[2018 Baliscan premiership election|2018 election]] of [[Secretary General of Balisca|Secretary General]] [[Andrea Palacios]], Vidal has partnered with the confederal government to replace all government vehicles with [[w:Plug-in electric vehicle|plug-in electric vehicles]] by 2021. This goal of an all-electric [[w:Fleet vehicle|government fleet]] was achieved in October 2020. Vidal accounted for 56% of the new plug-in market share in Balisca in 2019. 

